WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.905
Lady Whitebone sat by the road and sniffed the air again.

2
00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:12.901
"The Tang Monk has some powerful companions," she said.

3
00:00:12.902 --> 00:00:21.681
"I need a disguise."

4
00:00:21.682 --> 00:00:24.313
Bajie dropped the bags.

5
00:00:24.314 --> 00:00:26.802
[g@"I'm tired and hungry.

6
00:00:26.803 --> 00:00:30.688
Let's stop for lunch."@g]

7
00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:38.049
Using his magic sight, Wukong saw a peach orchard thousands of miles away.

8
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.981
"I'll be back in a minute," he said.

9
00:00:40.982 --> 00:00:47.076
Soon after the monkey had left, a young woman came down the road.

10
00:00:47.077 --> 00:00:49.878
She held out a bowl.

11
00:00:49.879 --> 00:00:53.025
[g@"Are you the Tang Monk?" she asked.

12
00:00:53.026 --> 00:00:55.552
"I have food for you."@g]

13
00:00:55.553 --> 00:01:00.661
Bajie reached for the bowl. "Thank you!"

14
00:01:00.662 --> 00:01:05.262
"Don't eat that!" Wukong was flying fast, back to the group.

15
00:01:05.263 --> 00:01:10.070
He dropped all the peaches and pulled out his iron bar.

16
00:01:10.071 --> 00:01:13.338
[i@Wham!@i] He struck at the young woman.

17
00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:19.337
But before he hit her, she disappeared.

18
00:01:19.338 --> 00:01:22.391
"Why did you do that?" cried the Tang Monk.

19
00:01:22.392 --> 00:01:25.782
"You're a human, Master," said Wukong.

20
00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:30.245
"You couldn't see that the woman was really a spirit who wanted to harm you.

21
00:01:30.246 --> 00:01:33.378
Unfortunately she got away."

22
00:01:33.379 --> 00:01:36.527
[g@"Why are you so cruel?" asked the monk.

23
00:01:36.528 --> 00:01:39.079
"She was giving us food."@g]

24
00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:45.186
"It's not food," said the monkey.

25
00:01:45.187 --> 00:01:51.520
"See?" He held up the bowl, which was filled with worms.

26
00:01:51.521 --> 00:01:54.828
"Don't believe Wukong," said Bajie.

27
00:01:54.829 --> 00:01:58.388
"He used magic to turn the food into worms."

28
00:01:58.389 --> 00:02:03.062
The pig looked at the ground where the woman had been and shook his head.

29
00:02:03.063 --> 00:02:07.880
"Wukong hit her so hard, there isn't anything left of her."

30
00:02:07.881 --> 00:02:15.958
"That's ridiculous," said Wukong. "I—ahh!"

31
00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:22.740
The monkey rolled on the ground as the Tang Monk recited the Tight Headband spell.

32
00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:27.889
Bajie laughed. "I didn't know you could do that, Master."

33
00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:31.954
Just then an old woman came down the road.

34
00:02:31.955 --> 00:02:38.776
The monk stopped reciting the spell, and Wukong stood up.

35
00:02:38.777 --> 00:02:42.811
"I'm looking for my daughter," said the woman.

36
00:02:42.812 --> 00:02:46.968
"She was bringing food to the Tang Monk."

37
00:02:46.969 --> 00:02:50.029
"Oh no," said the Tang Monk.

38
00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:52.659
Bajie stepped forward.

39
00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:56.511
"You should ask this monkey what happened to your daughter."

40
00:02:56.512 --> 00:03:03.196
Wukong looked at the old woman closely for a moment.

41
00:03:03.197 --> 00:03:07.128
[g@Then he took out his iron bar and swung.

42
00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:10.043
But again he missed.@g]

43
00:03:10.044 --> 00:03:14.134
"She got away again!" cried Wukong.

44
00:03:14.135 --> 00:03:18.384
"He killed another innocent person!" cried the pig.

45
00:03:18.385 --> 00:03:21.730
"Master, recite the spell!"

46
00:03:21.731 --> 00:03:25.142
[g@The Tang Monk recited the spell again.

47
00:03:25.143 --> 00:03:29.501
Wukong fell to the ground in pain.@g]

48
00:03:29.502 --> 00:03:33.729
"Please stop!" cried the monkey.

49
00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.613
[g@The Tang Monk stopped.

50
00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:39.203
"Don't hurt any more people," he said.@g]

51
00:03:39.204 --> 00:03:43.484
"If you do, I'll recite the spell until your head explodes."

52
00:03:43.485 --> 00:03:47.528
Just then an old man came down the road.

53
00:03:47.529 --> 00:03:54.583
"I'm looking for my wife and daughter," he said.

54
00:03:54.584 --> 00:03:58.609
"That's the evil spirit woman again," thought Wukong.

55
00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:02.669
"If I don't destroy her, she'll harm the Tang Monk.

56
00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:08.672
But if I do hurt her, the monk will make my head explode."

57
00:04:08.673 --> 00:04:15.794
Wukong sighed. "I must protect the Tang Monk, no matter what," he thought.

58
00:04:15.795 --> 00:04:20.187
[g@Wukong whipped out his iron bar and swung.

59
00:04:20.188 --> 00:04:22.853
There was a puff of smoke.@g]

60
00:04:22.854 --> 00:04:27.347
When the smoke cleared, a skeleton lay on the ground.

61
00:04:27.348 --> 00:04:29.775
[g@"I got her!" cried Wukong.

62
00:04:29.776 --> 00:04:33.604
"See? She was an evil skeleton spirit!"@g]

63
00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:35.795
The Tang Monk frowned.

64
00:04:35.796 --> 00:04:40.671
"Recite the spell again," Bajie said to the monk.

65
00:04:40.672 --> 00:04:44.467
"I want you to leave, Wukong," said the Tang Monk.

66
00:04:44.468 --> 00:04:49.551
"Master," said the monkey. "I just saved your life."

67
00:04:49.552 --> 00:04:52.107
"I don't believe you," said the monk.

68
00:04:52.108 --> 00:04:55.464
"Now leave or I'll recite the spell again."

69
00:04:55.465 --> 00:04:58.085
[g@Wukong became angry.

70
00:04:58.086 --> 00:05:01.339
"If you really want me to leave, I'll leave.@g]

71
00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:05.273
But don't come looking for me when you need help!"

72
00:05:05.274 --> 00:05:15.302
He leaped into the air and vanished.

